<DocsLayout title="Dependencies & extras" description="The scmle dependency policy: a light base install, optional extras that are never imported unless used, tested lower bounds, auditing and licence checks." current="dependencies">
  <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Reference</p>
  <h1>A light core,<br /><em>extras on request.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead">SCMLE needs CPython 3.11 or newer and is tested on 3.11, 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14, including the free-threaded 3.14 build. The base install is deliberately small, and nothing optional is imported unless you use it.</p>

  <h2>The base install</h2>
  <p>numpy, pandas, pyarrow, pydantic, scikit-learn, joblib and threadpoolctl. No GPU, service, database server or hosted account is required. The install commands are on the <a href={`${base}/docs/quickstart/`}>quickstart</a>.</p>

  <h2>Optional extras</h2>
  <DocTable label="Optional extras" head={["Extra", "Adds", "Notes"]} rows={extras} />
  <p>On macOS, the <code>boosting</code> extra needs the OpenMP runtime (<code>brew install libomp</code>). Which model families each extra enables, and which are experimental, is on the <a href={`${base}/docs/capabilities/`}>capability matrix</a>.</p>

  <h2>Version policy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No cloud SDK.</strong> No cloud-provider SDK and no SDK for a hosted-compute service is a dependency, a base requirement or an optional extra, and none may be added. Code that talks to a hosted service belongs to your own adapter, written against the interfaces the package ships.</li>
    <li><strong>Lower bounds are tested, not guessed.</strong> CI resolves the lowest direct versions and runs the unit, property and leakage suites on them (pandas 3.0, scikit-learn 1.8, numpy 2.3 and so on).</li>
    <li><strong>Upper bounds</strong> are not pinned in the library. The lock file records the combination that CI exercises.</li>
    <li><strong>Audit.</strong> <code>pip-audit</code> runs in CI; a vulnerable release fails the build.</li>
    <li><strong>Licences.</strong> The project is Apache-2.0. CI traverses the installed base runtime closure and publishes a licence inventory. A missing licence record or a copyleft licence (GPL, LGPL, AGPL, SSPL, BUSL or Elastic) fails the security job. Optional extras must be audited in the environment where they are enabled before a release claim includes them, and any copyleft package added to an extra needs review.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta">Dependency policy of the 0.1 beta line</p>
</DocsLayout>
